              "token": "SUMMARY",
              "label": "Contract summary",
              "type": "longtext",
              "value": "This Agreement is made between the Developer and the Client named above in respect of the project described herein. By signing, the Client confirms that the Client has reviewed and tested the delivered project in full and accepts it as working and complete. From the moment of signing, responsibility for the project, including any matter not covered by the Covered Services section of the Full Terms, rests with the Client. The Developer is not liable for any matter arising after acceptance that falls outside the promised services. The Client shall pay the agreed fee within three (3) days of signing; failure to do so may result in permanent suspension of the service. Lifetime customer support, as defined in the Full Terms, is available to the Client upon payment.",
              "min": 0,
              "max": 100,
              "step": 1
            },
            {
              "id": "ctlmut0r2ga88u",
              "token": "TERMS",
              "label": "Full terms (blank line between sections, first line = title)",
              "type": "longtext",
              "value": "1. Project Scope\nThe Developer builds a website that serves as a professional platform and bridge between the Client and the Client's own customers. Customers can view the Client's offers and submit their details, which are delivered securely to the Client, and the Client manages the website through the management site. The Client markets the website and personally performs all payment verification and fulfilment of orders. The service includes a review system and a live order status system.\n\n2. Client Testing & Acceptance\nBy signing, the Client confirms that the Client has tested every feature of the delivered project and that it works. Any issue discovered later that falls outside the promised services is the Client's responsibility, as it should have been identified during testing.\n\n3. Data & Privacy\nThe Developer does not store, sell, share or manage the Client's data or the Client's customers' data. The Client's Google account is used solely to verify identity and to set up the Client's website and its connected Google Sheet.\n\n4. Developer Responsibility\nAfter signing, the Developer is responsible only for providing future updates and advice, and for fixing defects in the Covered Services (Section 5). Future updates are chargeable; customer support is free (Section 8).\n\n5. Covered Services\nThe Developer is responsible for defects in: website functionality within the agreed scope; the front page; the review system; live order status; verification; the Client's customer verification; the data flow from the website to the Client's management Google Sheet; and any other functionality expressly promised. If these work as promised, the Developer has no further responsibility.\n\n6. Excluded Services\nThe Developer is not responsible for: any feature that was never promised; automatic payment processing (unless provided); automatic game-currency or item delivery; automatic currency exchange; problems caused by the Client's own modifications or misuse; new requirements; third-party or API changes; or anything the Client expected that was never part of the service. A customer entering game credentials does not trigger any automatic delivery by the website.\n\n7. Future Bugs & Maintenance\nBugs discovered after acceptance that are not within the Covered Services are the Client's responsibility. To have such issues fixed, the Client must engage the Developer as a new client under a new agreement.\n\n8. Customer Support\nThe Developer provides free customer support for the delivered project for the lifetime of the Developer's business, application and platform. If the business or the personal brand ceases to exist, support ends. Support covers the delivered project only; new features and modifications are chargeable.\n\n9. Changes & Modifications\nThe Developer will help with modifications during the first three (3) days after signing. After that period, all changes and any consequences of them are the Client's responsibility.\n\n10. Hosting, Domain & API Costs\nThe project currently requires no hosting cost. A custom domain is optional and at the Client's expense; the Developer can connect it. There are currently no API costs, but any that arise in future are payable by the Client.\n\n11. Payment Obligations\nThe agreed fee must be paid within three (3) days of signing. The Client may pay in advance or at any time within that period. Paid clients receive lifetime customer support as described in Section 8. The price is as separately agreed between the parties and is not stated in this document.\n\n12. Service Suspension\nIf payment is not received within three (3) days of signing, the Developer may permanently disable the Client's website.\n\n13. Refunds\nA refund, or a free fix, is given only where a service expressly described in this document is found not to work. Matters not covered by this document, and issues the Client should have identified during testing, are not eligible for a refund.\n\n14. Ownership\nOwnership of the finished project passes to the Client three (3) days after signing, and the Client may then edit and modify it.\n\n15. Limitation of Liability\nThe Developer's liability is limited to fixing, free of charge, any major defect in a service this document states the project provides. New issues that the Client did not test or anticipate are the Client's responsibility.\n\n16. Electronic Signature & Verification\nThe Client's identity is verified through Google Sign-In. The Client's typed name and chosen signature (typed or drawn), together with the date, time and device details, form the Client's electronic signature. The Client's optional note is informational only and does not alter this Agreement.\n\n17. Governing Law\nThis Agreement is governed by the laws of the People's Republic of Bangladesh.\n\n18. Acceptance\nBy signing, the Client accepts this document in full, including all rules and terms, and the policy at the link provided.",
